Fifty-two years. That’s how long the Léopards have been waiting to step back onto the World Cup stage. Since nineteen seventy-four. And to witness this to watch my country return brings a joy I can’t even put into words.

Fun fact: Congo holds over seventy percent of the world’s cobalt. The mineral that powers every device in your hand. But what powers me right now is watching the Leopards roar again on football’s biggest stage!

